{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Southwell1999-three-contiguous-stacks",
  "Source": "W. H. Southwell, \"Omnidirectional mirror design with quarter-wave dielectric stacks,\" Appl. Opt. 38, 5464-5467 (1999). doi:10.1364/AO.38.005464 - Fig. 7 caption (prescription) and p. 5467 text",
  "Notes": "Omnidirectional mirror with three contiguous quarter-wave stacks positioned by Eq. (7)\nSpecification: Further broadening of the omnidirectional band with a third stack.\nReported: Fig. 7: R at normal incidence (solid) and p at 85 deg (dashed), 6-20 um; normal-incidence high-R band roughly 6.7-17.5 um, p 85 deg roughly 7-15.5 um (read off plot), i.e. a further broadened omnidirectional band.\nNotes: AIR (LH)^10 1.0992L 1.1984(HL)^9 1.1984H 1.317L 1.436(HL)^9 1.4736H SUB, expanded: 10 x (L H), 1.0992L, 9 x (1.1984H 1.1984L), 1.1984H, 1.317L, 9 x (1.436H 1.436L), 1.4736H = 60 layers, L next to air. 1.436 = 1.1984^2 (Eq. 7) and 1.317 = (1.1984 + 1.436)/2. The final 1.4736H is transcribed as printed although the stack pattern suggests 1.436H (possible misprint); the effect on the band is small.\nLayers from Fig. 7 caption (prescription) and p. 5467 text; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), compare with the paper: ours min(Rs, Rp) 0.999927 over 0-89 deg at 9 um; paper wider all-angle band (Figs. 6-7, plots only).",
  "Wavelength": [
    10000
  ],
